WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.299 --> 00:00:05.070
Who among us hasn’t wondered what happens
after our lives have come to their inevitable

00:00:05.070 --> 00:00:09.010
ending, and we play out our final moments
in the land of the living?

00:00:09.010 --> 00:00:14.080
The concept of what happens to us after we’ve
died has baffled scientists and philosophers

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:19.050
the world over for almost as long as human
civilization has existed.

00:00:19.050 --> 00:00:22.220
Some out there already claim to know the exact
answer.

00:00:22.220 --> 00:00:26.669
You probably already know that the belief
in the existence of an afterlife is one held

00:00:26.669 --> 00:00:33.730
by almost every single religion and culture
around the globe; Heaven, Hell, Valhalla,

00:00:33.730 --> 00:00:37.850
Purgatory, Limbo, Sheol, the World to Come.

00:00:37.850 --> 00:00:42.190
Descriptions of the afterlife, and how to
get sent there, often varies depending on

00:00:42.190 --> 00:00:44.879
the religion or cultural group it is linked
to.

00:00:44.879 --> 00:00:49.899
But to think in more general terms, the concept
usually revolves around the soul leaving the

00:00:49.899 --> 00:00:54.399
body after death, and living forever in eternal
paradise.

00:00:54.399 --> 00:00:59.820
That is, of course, unless you’ve committed
any deadly sins during your lifetime.

00:00:59.820 --> 00:01:05.000
If the myths are to be believed, these normally
result in you being sent down to spend eternity

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:08.790
in damnation and endless punishment instead
of paradise.

00:01:08.790 --> 00:01:13.820
Sadly, there’s no way to prove if any of
the various afterlives actually exist.

00:01:13.820 --> 00:01:18.430
By their very nature, these afterlives exist
separate from the real, physical world that

00:01:18.430 --> 00:01:20.790
we live in while we are still alive.

00:01:20.790 --> 00:01:27.060
While we’re here on Earth, we can only observe
what we see happening to a body after death,

00:01:27.060 --> 00:01:31.020
and what we assume or believe the afterlife
might be like.

00:01:31.020 --> 00:01:36.250
After all, it’s not like any deceased person
can tell us what being dead is like… well,

00:01:36.250 --> 00:01:39.130
not under the normal circumstances anyway.

00:01:39.130 --> 00:01:43.680
With no proof of the afterlife’s existence,
we do unfortunately get left with the bleak

00:01:43.680 --> 00:01:48.500
and existentially terrifying assumption that,
when we die, there is nothing waiting for

00:01:48.500 --> 00:01:50.300
us on the other side.

00:01:50.300 --> 00:01:56.240
What if there’s no light at the end of the
tunnel, no pearly gates, just… nothing,

00:01:56.240 --> 00:01:57.240
forever?

00:01:57.240 --> 00:02:02.750
But what if someone, or some mysterious group
of persons, already knew the answer to what

00:02:02.750 --> 00:02:05.670
happened after the end of all human life?

00:02:05.670 --> 00:02:10.700
And what if the answer was so much more horrifying
than we ever could have imagined, so much

00:02:10.700 --> 00:02:15.420
so that this shadowy cabal had already tried
to prevent the fate awaiting all of us after

00:02:15.420 --> 00:02:16.420
we die?

00:02:16.420 --> 00:02:21.340
Be warned, we’re about to delve into the
unsettling tale of something known as Project

00:02:21.340 --> 00:02:28.670
Dammerung, and its connection to something
known as SCP-3448, as the Foundation categorizes

00:02:28.670 --> 00:02:29.670
it.

00:02:29.670 --> 00:02:35.480
It’s a story about our fear of what comes
next, beyond this mortal coil.

00:02:35.480 --> 00:02:40.440
This is the catalyst for the Foundation uncovering
the most horrific secret in human history,

00:02:40.440 --> 00:02:43.450
a truth that should have stayed buried.

00:02:43.450 --> 00:02:47.360
Warning - We are about to unravel the beginning
of the end.

00:02:47.360 --> 00:02:48.680
“The end of what?”

00:02:48.680 --> 00:02:49.850
you might be asking.

00:02:49.850 --> 00:02:53.480
Why, the End of Death itself, of course.

00:02:53.480 --> 00:02:57.770
Any outsider looking in might think we’re
being a little bit over-dramatic here, but

00:02:57.770 --> 00:03:01.819
we’ll forgive you for that mistake, you
can have that one on us.

00:03:01.819 --> 00:03:08.200
At first glance, to the untrained eye and
uninformed individual, SCP-3448 might just

00:03:08.200 --> 00:03:12.160
seem like little more than a Magnetic Resonance
Imaging machine, or an MRI for short.

00:03:12.160 --> 00:03:16.330
Chances are you’ve seen these big machines
in medical dramas, or maybe you’ve even

00:03:16.330 --> 00:03:19.650
been placed inside one during a stay at the
hospital.

00:03:19.650 --> 00:03:24.280
Using powerful magnets, an MRI machine aligns
all the protons in your body.

00:03:24.280 --> 00:03:29.190
Then, the machine generates a pulse of radiofrequency
current to create a detailed image of the

00:03:29.190 --> 00:03:31.280
inside of a patient’s body.

00:03:31.280 --> 00:03:36.450
Basically, to put it in extremely oversimplified
terms, it’s a big camera for looking at

00:03:36.450 --> 00:03:37.710
your internal organs.

00:03:37.710 --> 00:03:42.540
Now, don’t forget to smile, really show
off that pancreas, it looks great at this

00:03:42.540 --> 00:03:43.540
angle!

00:03:43.540 --> 00:03:47.540
Of course, when dealing with anomalies encountered
by the SCP Foundation, few things are ever

00:03:47.540 --> 00:03:49.860
really exactly as they first seem.

00:03:49.860 --> 00:03:55.709
And in that very same vein, SCP-3448 is far
more than just a harmless piece of medical

00:03:55.709 --> 00:03:56.760
apparatus.

00:03:56.760 --> 00:04:01.350
Look beyond the main bulk of the MRI machine
and you’ll start to notice that a few unique

00:04:01.350 --> 00:04:03.760
modifications have been made to the device.

00:04:03.760 --> 00:04:09.130
For one, the winding mass of jumper cables
connecting the machine to its rudimentary

00:04:09.130 --> 00:04:14.510
upgrades, namely the same type of technology
used in particle accelerators, along with

00:04:14.510 --> 00:04:17.209
a whole collection of custom circuit boards.

00:04:17.209 --> 00:04:22.500
For another, although you wouldn’t know
just from looking at SCP-3448, the contraption

00:04:22.500 --> 00:04:27.620
has also been through a number of anomalous
rituals, seemingly combining the technological

00:04:27.620 --> 00:04:30.090
with the occult and spiritual.

00:04:30.090 --> 00:04:32.819
But the question remains: why?

00:04:32.819 --> 00:04:35.080
What is this thing for exactly?

00:04:35.080 --> 00:04:39.610
To put it simply, it’s a hotline to the
great beyond.

00:04:39.610 --> 00:04:44.939
SCP-3448 is a means of communication with
the world of the dead themselves.

00:04:44.939 --> 00:04:50.900
Now, we might be oversimplifying things yet
again there, so let’s take it from the top.

00:04:50.900 --> 00:04:55.370
Project Dammerung was the name given to those
who developed SCP-3448.

00:04:55.370 --> 00:05:00.389
That designation doesn’t just refer to the
modified MRI machine itself, but also the

00:05:00.389 --> 00:05:05.240
communication that said device was capable
of after the Project Dammerung team had finished

00:05:05.240 --> 00:05:06.650
their tinkering with it.

00:05:06.650 --> 00:05:11.839
You see, nobody knows what happens to us after
we die, because no one has ever been able

00:05:11.839 --> 00:05:17.059
to experience being dead in the real world
and existing in the afterlife at the same

00:05:17.059 --> 00:05:18.059
time.

00:05:18.059 --> 00:05:24.539
But with SCP-3448, that problem just simply
isn’t an issue anymore.

00:05:24.539 --> 00:05:25.660
Still with us so far?

00:05:25.660 --> 00:05:28.469
Okay, here’s how the machine actually works.

00:05:28.469 --> 00:05:33.789
A living human is placed inside, just like
those ordinary MRI machines at your local

00:05:33.789 --> 00:05:34.789
hospital.

00:05:34.789 --> 00:05:40.539
However, the difference here is that the extra,
anomalous components of SCP-3448 – the rituals,

00:05:40.539 --> 00:05:45.439
the particle acceleration, and so on – allow
this person to enter a unique state of being

00:05:45.439 --> 00:05:48.089
halfway between life and death.

00:05:48.089 --> 00:05:51.610
Their bodily functions are halted, brought
to a stop by the machine.

00:05:51.610 --> 00:05:56.610
However, they are still able to retain their
consciousness and the awareness that this

00:05:56.610 --> 00:05:58.039
allows for.

00:05:58.039 --> 00:06:04.659
Not quite dead, but not quite alive either,
sort of an ‘unalive’ state or a half-death,

00:06:04.659 --> 00:06:05.800
if you prefer.

00:06:05.800 --> 00:06:07.619
Or perhaps...Halfterlife.

00:06:07.619 --> 00:06:12.889
Now, while a person is in this half-death,
they will have entered a conceptual state

00:06:12.889 --> 00:06:14.020
of being.

00:06:14.020 --> 00:06:21.460
This is referred to as SCP-3448-A, an existence
of pure consciousness while physical form,

00:06:21.460 --> 00:06:25.960
in this case, the person’s body, exists
separately in the real world.

00:06:25.960 --> 00:06:32.650
The body, now called SCP-3448-1, no longer
houses a subject’s consciousness, their

00:06:32.650 --> 00:06:33.880
essence.

00:06:33.880 --> 00:06:37.050
Not just their mind but their thoughts and
personality.

00:06:37.050 --> 00:06:42.300
If it helps to think of it in theological
terms, you could even think of it as their

00:06:42.300 --> 00:06:43.300
soul.

00:06:43.300 --> 00:06:47.169
But, while the machine’s function is all
very impressive and interesting, what’s

00:06:47.169 --> 00:06:48.930
the actual point to it?

00:06:48.930 --> 00:06:52.529
Why spend so much time trying to create a
controlled separation of consciousness from

00:06:52.529 --> 00:06:53.800
a dead body?

00:06:53.800 --> 00:06:55.729
What’s Project Dammerung for?

00:06:55.729 --> 00:06:58.370
Well, that’s easy.

00:06:58.370 --> 00:07:04.190
SCP-3448 is the primary tool intended to complete
the sole objective of Project Dammerung, a

00:07:04.190 --> 00:07:10.120
mission to capture a dangerous cognitohazard:
namely, death itself.

00:07:10.120 --> 00:07:15.279
To be clear, when we say “death”, we don’t
mean the Grim Reaper, that skull-faced, scythe-wielding

00:07:15.279 --> 00:07:17.340
embodiment of oblivion.

00:07:17.340 --> 00:07:21.599
Chances are, you can probably catch him just
by going out on Halloween with a big net.

00:07:21.599 --> 00:07:27.169
But Project Dammerung’s goal was to contain
the actual process of death, the very concept

00:07:27.169 --> 00:07:31.490
that takes a living, conscious entity and
makes it the opposite.

00:07:31.490 --> 00:07:36.659
You see, when a living subject is placed in
SCP-3448 and their consciousness leaves their

00:07:36.659 --> 00:07:41.150
brain, it leaves behind some kind of anomalous
electrical energy signature.

00:07:41.150 --> 00:07:46.020
As you may already know if you can remember
back to high school Biology class, the brain

00:07:46.020 --> 00:07:52.210
uses electrical impulses to send signals all
over the body, allowing your organs to function,

00:07:52.210 --> 00:07:56.319
your limbs to move, and your muscles to contract
or relax.

00:07:56.319 --> 00:08:02.199
What’s strange is, this electrical activity
seems to continue within the brain of someone

00:08:02.199 --> 00:08:07.409
whose consciousness has been separated from
their body by SCP-3448.

00:08:07.409 --> 00:08:12.289
Studying these signals, the SCP Foundation
personnel working on Project Dammerung have

00:08:12.289 --> 00:08:17.210
inferred that these are residual signals,
replicating how the brain would react if the

00:08:17.210 --> 00:08:24.129
subject introduced into the half-dead SCP-3448-1
state as if they were still alive, even though

00:08:24.129 --> 00:08:28.319
they have to be dead in order to access that
state in the first place.

00:08:28.319 --> 00:08:32.370
And now your brain is probably such a mess
of electrical signals trying to keep up with

00:08:32.370 --> 00:08:37.569
all that, that you might have completely missed
the part where we told you that Project Dammerung

00:08:37.569 --> 00:08:40.860
is actually a Foundation-backed project.

00:08:40.860 --> 00:08:43.529
Okay, let’s have a speedy recap.

00:08:43.529 --> 00:08:48.370
So far, we have an anomalously modified MRI
machine, capable of splitting the consciousness,

00:08:48.370 --> 00:08:51.709
or soul, of a person after rendering them
clinically dead.

00:08:51.709 --> 00:08:55.440
On top of that, the Foundation themselves
sanctioned the project that created this device

00:08:55.440 --> 00:08:58.569
in an effort to capture and contain death
itself.

00:08:58.569 --> 00:09:00.779
But, how did this come about?

00:09:00.779 --> 00:09:06.380
Who among the SCP Foundation would want to
contain death, so much to commission an entire

00:09:06.380 --> 00:09:08.589
project dedicated to that goal?

00:09:08.589 --> 00:09:14.380
Well, who do we all know sitting above the
entire Foundation, overseeing everything,

00:09:14.380 --> 00:09:20.339
infamous for all having some anomalous form
of immortality, and would stand to gain from

00:09:20.339 --> 00:09:21.529
Project Dammerung?

00:09:21.529 --> 00:09:27.520
That’s right, the world championship death
dodgers: The O5 Council.

00:09:27.520 --> 00:09:32.210
You see, in order to more fully understand
why Project Dammerung was established, and

00:09:32.210 --> 00:09:40.870
why they built SCP-3448, we need to explain
a little bit about a different anomaly: SCP-2718.

00:09:40.870 --> 00:09:44.780
We have another video on this channel that
goes into more detail about that, but to put

00:09:44.780 --> 00:09:51.240
it in a nutshell, SCP-2718 is the horrible
truth about what happens to us after we die.

00:09:51.240 --> 00:09:56.980
The O5 Council first learned of it when one
of their own, O5-11, full name Roger Sheldon,

00:09:56.980 --> 00:09:58.700
died of a stroke.

00:09:58.700 --> 00:10:03.959
O5-11 was the only council member to have
refused to accept any of the anomalous treatments

00:10:03.959 --> 00:10:07.620
or enhancements that prevented the other O5s
from dying.

00:10:07.620 --> 00:10:10.420
However, the council chose to resurrect him.

00:10:10.420 --> 00:10:15.160
Upon his return to the land of the living,
Roger Sheldon told the other overseers what

00:10:15.160 --> 00:10:20.720
he had learned about the nature of the afterlife,
what lies beyond this fleeting mortal coil,

00:10:20.720 --> 00:10:22.760
waiting for us after we die.

00:10:22.760 --> 00:10:28.430
Roger had experienced firsthand that the dead
actually remain conscious after their bodies

00:10:28.430 --> 00:10:31.440
have shut down all other functions.

00:10:31.440 --> 00:10:36.940
That meant that everyone, every person to
have died over the course of human history,

00:10:36.940 --> 00:10:41.360
has remained aware of everything that happened
to them afterward.

00:10:41.360 --> 00:10:47.080
They can feel themselves slowly decaying,
their bones and skin withering, buried under

00:10:47.080 --> 00:10:51.930
the cold, wasting away into nothingness day
after day.

00:10:51.930 --> 00:11:01.250
And that’s SCP-2718, the painful truth that
there is no paradise, no heaven, no afterlife.

00:11:01.250 --> 00:11:07.269
There is just endless, silent consciousness
beyond the end of every life.

00:11:07.269 --> 00:11:13.149
This revelation is what instigated the overseer
council, specifically O5-4, to establish Project

00:11:13.149 --> 00:11:14.149
Dammerung.

00:11:14.149 --> 00:11:19.990
It was learning the answer to ‘what happens
next’ that spurred the creation of SCP-3448.

00:11:19.990 --> 00:11:24.389
The intention was, by reading and interacting
with those residual electrical signals in

00:11:24.389 --> 00:11:29.649
the brain, that the Foundation could create
a link, a form of two-way communication between

00:11:29.649 --> 00:11:37.130
them in the living world and the subject,
SCP-3448-A, in their half-dead state.

00:11:37.130 --> 00:11:41.899
Using other items’ anomalous technology
connected to the MRI machine, the Foundation’s

00:11:41.899 --> 00:11:47.970
researchers could interpret the electrical
signals in SCP-3448-A’s brain as images.

00:11:47.970 --> 00:11:52.720
A Foundation agent by the name of Anthony
Michaels proved to be the only test subject

00:11:52.720 --> 00:11:58.410
capable of using SCP-3448, beyond the earliest
tests on animal specimens.

00:11:58.410 --> 00:12:03.350
And we know what you’re thinking, the Foundation
would normally use D-Class personnel for this

00:12:03.350 --> 00:12:04.730
sort of test.

00:12:04.730 --> 00:12:09.250
After all, it’s a machine that renders you
almost dead, stopping all bodily function.

00:12:09.250 --> 00:12:14.269
The problem was, Project Dammerung needed
someone loyal to the Foundation, and D-Classes

00:12:14.269 --> 00:12:18.139
could hardly be trusted to follow orders without
the threat of death.

00:12:18.139 --> 00:12:21.759
Think about it, you separate their consciousness
from their body and they don’t care if you

00:12:21.759 --> 00:12:23.350
threaten to kill them.

00:12:23.350 --> 00:12:30.519
Agent Michaels served as the SCP-3448-A component,
residing within the modified MRI machine,

00:12:30.519 --> 00:12:33.240
held in a state between life and death.

00:12:33.240 --> 00:12:38.950
But something went wrong, something that would
ultimately do more harm than good.

00:12:38.950 --> 00:12:44.009
The Foundation had tried in vain to contain
death, and in tampering with forces well beyond

00:12:44.009 --> 00:12:49.459
their own understanding, may have accidentally
done something even worse.

00:12:49.459 --> 00:12:51.220
They neutralised it.

00:12:51.220 --> 00:12:57.050
They killed death, and things only went downhill
from there...

00:12:57.050 --> 00:13:03.430
Now go check out “Evil Monster Created by
SCP Foundation SCP-2419 - The Laughing Men”

00:13:03.430 --> 00:13:09.000
and “SCP-006 - Fountain of Youth” for
more SCPs that blur the line between life

00:13:09.000 --> 00:13:09.130
and death!

